[al:新概念英语（三）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Do It Yourself]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:00.49]Lesson 46 | 第46课
[00:02.61]Do it yourself | 自己动手
[00:09.29]Did the writer repair his lawn mower in the end? Why/Why not? | 作者最终修好割草机了吗？为什么？
[00:16.95]So great is our passion for doing things for ourselves, | 我们是如此热衷于自己动手，
[00:21.40]that we are becoming increasingly less dependent on specialized labour. | 以至于对专业劳动的依赖日益减少。
[00:27.22]No one can plead ignorance of a subject any longer, for there are countless do-it-yourself publications. | 谁也不能再借口对某事一无所知，因为有数不清的“自己动手”出版物。
[00:35.22]Armed with the right tools and materials, newlyweds gaily embark on the task of decorating their own homes. | 备好了合适的工具和材料，新婚夫妇们便兴致勃勃地开始装饰自己的新房。
[00:43.70]Men, particularly, spend hours of their leisure time installing their own fireplaces, | 尤其是男人们，把闲暇时间的大量时间花在安装自家的壁炉、
[00:50.59]laying out their own gardens; building garages and making furniture. | 布置自家的花园、建造车库和制作家具上。
[00:56.23]Some really keen enthusiasts go so far as to build their own computers. | 一些真正的狂热分子甚至亲手组装自己的电脑。
[01:02.48]Shops cater for the do-it-yourself craze not only by running special advisory services for novices, | 商店迎合这种自己动手的狂热，不仅为新手开设特别的咨询服务，
[01:10.21]but by offering consumers bits and pieces which they can assemble at home. | 而且向消费者出售可以在家里组装的零配件。
[01:15.74]Such things provide an excellent outlet for pent up creative energy, but unfortunately not all of us are born handymen. | 这类事情为被压抑的创造力提供了极好的发泄途径，但不幸的是，我们并非人人都是天生的巧匠。
[01:26.47]Some wives tend to believe that their husbands are infinitely resourceful and can fix anything. | 有些妻子倾向于认为丈夫无所不能，什么都能修。
[01:33.94]Even men who can hardly drive a nail in straight are supposed to be born electricians, carpenters, plumbers and mechanics. | 甚至连连钉子都钉不直的男人也被认为生来就是电工、木匠、管道工和机械师。
[01:43.52]When lights fuse, furniture gets rickety, pipes get clogged, or vacuum cleaners fail to operate, | 当保险丝烧断、家具摇晃、管道堵塞或吸尘器无法运转时，
[01:51.83]some women assume that their husbands will somehow put things right. | 有些女人便以为丈夫总会想办法把它们修好。
[01:56.51]The worst thing about the do-it-yourself game is that sometimes even men live under the delusion that they can do anything, | 自己动手这个游戏最糟糕的一点是，有时甚至连男人也生活在自己什么都能干的错觉之中，
[02:05.20]even when they have repeatedly been proved wrong. | 尽管他们已一再被证明并非如此。
[02:09.05]It is a question of pride as much as anything else. | 这在很大程度上是个面子问题。
[02:13.10]Last spring my wife suggested that I call in a man to look at our lawn mower. | 去年春天，妻子建议我请人来检修我们的割草机。
[02:19.30]It had broken down the previous summer, and though I promised to repair it, I had never got round to it. | 它前一年夏天就坏了，虽然我答应修理，却一直没腾出工夫来。
[02:27.78]I would not hear of the suggestion and said that I would fix it myself. | 我不听这个建议，说自己来修。
[02:33.70]One Saturday afternoon, I hauled the machine into the garden and had a close look at it. | 一个星期六的下午，我把机器拖到花园里，仔细察看了一番。
[02:40.45]As far as I could see, it needed only a minor adjustment: | 据我看，它只需要稍微调整一下：
[02:45.27]a turn of a screw here, a little tightening up there, a drop of oil and it would be as good as new. | 这儿拧一下螺丝，那儿紧一紧，加一滴油，它就会像新的一样了。
[02:53.88]Inevitably the repair job was not quite so simple. | 修理工作不可避免地并不那么简单。
[02:59.04]The mower firmly refused to mow, so I decided to dismantle it. | 割草机倔强地拒绝割草，于是我决定把它拆开。
[03:05.22]The garden was soon littered with chunks of metal which had once made up a lawn mower. | 很快，花园里就散落着曾经组成一台割草机的大块小块的金属。
[03:12.99]But I was extremely pleased with myself. I had traced the cause of the trouble. | 但我自我感觉非常好：我已经找到了故障的原因。
[03:18.61]One of the links in the chain that drives the wheels had snapped. | 驱动轮子的链条断了一环。
[03:23.64]After buying a new chain I was faced with the insurmountable task of putting the confusing jigsaw puzzle together again. | 买了新链条之后，我便面临把这个令人困惑的拼图玩具重新拼装起来的难以应付的任务。
[03:34.70]I was not surprised to find that the machine still refused to work after I had reassembled it, | 重新组装之后，机器仍然拒绝运转，对此我并不感到意外，
[03:42.35]for the simple reason that I was left with several curiously shaped bits of metal which did not seem to fit anywhere. | 原因很简单：我手里剩下几块形状古怪的金属，似乎哪儿也装不上。
[03:52.44]I gave up in despair. | 我绝望地放弃了。
[03:55.01]The weeks passed and the grass grew. | 几个星期过去了，草长了起来。
[03:58.12]When my wife nagged me to do something about it, | 当妻子喋喋不休地让我想想办法时，
[04:01.52]I told her that either I would have to buy a new mower or let the grass grow. | 我告诉她说，要么买台新割草机，要么就让草长下去。
[04:06.91]Needless to say our house is now surrounded by a jungle. | 不用说，我们家如今被一片丛林包围着。
[04:11.75]Buried somewhere in deep grass there is a rusting lawn mower which I have promised to repair one day. | 在深草丛中的某个地方，埋藏着一台生了锈的割草机，我答应过哪天要把它修好。
